\begin{aligned}
n + b &= 2.4, \\
a + m &= 5.1.
\end{aligned}
\]
From the first equation, we have \(n = \lfloor x \rfloor\) and \(b = \{y\}\). From the second equation, we have \(a = \{x\}\) and \(m = \lfloor y \rfloor\). Since \(a\) and \(b\) are fractional parts, \(0 \leq a, b < 1\). Therefore, \(n\) and \(m\) are integers such that \(n \leq 2.4 < n+1\) and \(m \leq 5.1 < m+1\). This means \(n = 2\) and \(m = 5\). Substituting these into the equations, we get \[
\begin{aligned}
2 + b &= 2.4 \implies b = 0.4, \\
a + 5 &= 5.1 \implies a = 0.1.
\end{aligned}
\]
So, \(x = 2 + 0.1 = 2.1\) and \(y = 5 + 0.4 = 5.4\). The absolute difference is \(|x - y| = |2.1 - 5.4| = 3.3\). </think> <answer> 3.3 </answer>

